## 5. Core Abilities

The following abilities form the initial ability set for the game. Each ability has a unique archetype that encourages different playstyles.

### 5.1 Berserker

| Property | Value |
|----------|-------|
| Trigger | `onAttack` |
| Effect | Gain +1 ATK (temporary, lasts until end of battle) |
| Target | Self |
| Scaling | Level 1: +1 ATK \| Level 2: +2 ATK \| Level 3: +3 ATK |
| Archetype | Scaling Attacker |

**Design Intent:** Berserker rewards survival. The longer it stays alive, the more dangerous it becomes. Best positioned in the back so it can build up attack stacks before reaching the front line. Synergizes with pets that provide shields or healing.

**Implementation Notes:** The ATK bonus is temporary and tracked per-battle. Reset the bonus at the start of each new battle. Store `attackCount` on the pet instance during combat.

### 5.2 Echo

| Property | Value |
|----------|-------|
| Trigger | `startOfBattle` |
| Effect | Deal 3 damage to a random enemy. Repeats for each battle this pet has participated in. |
| Target | Random enemy |
| Scaling | Level 1: 3 damage \| Level 2: 4 damage \| Level 3: 5 damage per echo |
| Archetype | Snowball / Veteran |

**Design Intent:** Echo is a long-term investment. Early purchase yields massive late-game value. A pet bought on Turn 1 that survives to Turn 10 would deal 10×3=30 damage at battle start (Level 1). Creates interesting decisions around protecting this pet vs. selling for stronger options.

**Implementation Notes:** Track `battlesParticipated` as a persistent counter on the pet. Increment after each battle phase (win or lose). This counter persists across shop phases and is part of the pet's saved state.

### 5.3 Pure

| Property | Value |
|----------|-------|
| Trigger | `onFaint` |
| Effect | Heal all surviving allies for 3 HP |
| Target | All friendly pets currently in battle |
| Scaling | Level 1: 3 HP \| Level 2: 5 HP \| Level 3: 7 HP |
| Archetype | Sacrifice / Support |

**Design Intent:** Pure rewards deliberate sacrifice. Position it to die at a strategic moment when allies are damaged. Creates counter-play against chip damage strategies and sniper abilities. Can save a run when combined with high-HP tanks.

**Implementation Notes:** Healing cannot exceed max HP (50). Trigger after the pet is removed from battle but before the next attack resolves. Does not heal pets that faint simultaneously with this pet.

